True division uses / and always returns a float. Floor division // gives the whole-number quotient instead."}

Worked example (from the reading):
if temp > 100: print('boiling') else: print('not boiling')
Discuss execution: only one branch runs. Then connect boolean logic: temp > 100 by itself is a single condition; later we’ll combine conditions with and/or and invert with not. Use the quote “When an if-else statement is executed, one and only one of the branches is taken” to emphasize mutual exclusivity.
